// Title: when the serial node-walk is contained (its activation budget) or
// honestly slow, the forked JIT (Mode::JitPar) is compared with nothing that
// ran: Pair::Par(JitPar)'s reference is the serial node-walk, and no pair
// holds the forked JIT to the serial JIT.
// Command: timeout -s KILL 180 graphix-fuzz check fuzz-lib-a-forked-jit-unrefuted.gx
//          timeout -s KILL 180 graphix-fuzz run fuzz-lib-a-forked-jit-unrefuted.gx
// Expected: the serial JIT's trace (100000, [2, 4, ..]) is the forked JIT's
// reference once the node-walk cannot answer; a forked-JIT bug here diverges.
// Observed: `run` shows Interp Timeout(ActivationBudget), Jit Trace; `check`
// prints two "CONTAINED — the node-walk exceeded its stack or activation
// budget; the kernel's value stands unrefuted" lines (Pair::Engine and
// Pair::Par(JitPar)) and ends UNSURE: the JitPar run's value is never
// compared with the serial JIT's.
let rec f = |n: i64, acc: i64| -> i64 select n { 0 => acc, n => f(n - 1, acc + 1) };
let xs = array::map([1, 2, 3, 4, 5, 6, 7, 8], |x| x * 2);
(f(100000, 0), xs)
